          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+objects"} free objects
            in “algebraic” categories. The idea is that one has to start from some “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"}> generators
            ” and repeatedly throw in the results of applying “operations”, subject to some “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"}> relations
            ”, over and over again until the result “converges”. In general, this convergence will require a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+number"} transfinite
            iteration, and the fact that it converges at all requires some smallness/accessibility hypotheses.
          %p If this construction is performed in sufficient generality, then it includes a large number of important special cases, such as the following (not mutually exclusive):
          %ul
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monad"} free monad
              generated by an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monad"} free monad
              generated by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+endofunctor"} pointed endofunctor
            %li
              the free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              generated by an object of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorization+system"} orthogonal factorization system
              generated by a set of morphisms
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflectiveness
              of a
              %span.newWikiWord
                small-orthogonality class
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/orthogonality+class"} ?
            %li
              the reflectiveness of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              preserving certain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocompleteness
              of the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
              for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %li
              the existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
              to functors between categories of algebras for monads
            %li the existence of colimits for diagrams of monads
            %li the existence of colimits in categories of monoids
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+small+object+argument"} algebraic small object argument
              generating
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+weak+factorization+systems"} algebraic weak factorization systems
            %li
              the existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-types"} W-types
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
              in categories
            %li
              the existence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
              in categories
          %p
            In 1980,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"} Max Kelly
            %a{:href => "#Kelly"} (Kelly)
            wrote a very long paper detailing very precise and general conditions under which such constructions can be performed, and showing how they can all be reduced to the case of free algebras for
            = succeed "." do
              %em well-pointed endofunctors
          %p
            In what follows we will summarize Kelly’s constructions, restricted to the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functors"} accessible functors
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
